{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/987860-exalted-3e-exigents-perfect-for-rwby-game","id":987860,"title":"Exalted 3e: Exigents Perfect for RWBY game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-15T11:45:40-07:00","id":987860,"title":"Exalted 3e: Exigents Perfect for RWBY game","content":"So after watching the trailer for the new season for RWBY I began thinking how could I twist a system to capture the feel for that world. Exalted 3e was the answer. Exigents are perfect set their power levels and essence at around a dragonblooded for the beginning of a chronicle and after a major breakthrough as a character or story arc &quot;exalt&quot; them to the level of a celestial exalt like lunar.<br /> Exigents being tied to a single concept is a great one for one with semblances.<br /> Sorcery could be changed to instead of having an infinite amount of essence to draw on you can only draw on the Dust you have on you with a surcharge of using up one or two of your personal essence points. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:15:49-07:00","id":987877,"title":"","content":"I think Creation's Fire Dust and Remnant's Fire Dust could be conflated into the same thing.<br /> <br /> You need a certainly level of the Resources Merit to justify having a steady supply of Fire Dust, but you can learn Charms other than the Righteous Devil Style for using that substance to perform fiery magical tricks.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:09:38-07:00","id":987952,"title":"","content":"I was thinking you would have units of dust with each unit worth one sorcery mote. With depending on where in remant the party is could make dust worth more or less also dust would be used in mecha shift weapons which could use artifact rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:08:09-07:00","id":988148,"title":"","content":"Well the way I see it Aura users largely behave as skill based exalts.<br /> <br /> However They have no anima effects, although they do have displays, their anima flares based on use of their semblance instead of mote use. They'd have only a large personal mote pool.<br /> <br /> Every Aura user would have access to Evocation type powers form their dust-tech gear which includes their mecha-shift weaponry and covers things from dust infused clothes to basic dust bullets to flying laser rifle swords to cameras that create temporary copies of other weapons to vehicles and mecha.<br /> <br /> Direct Aura control, their personal protective fields, regen factor, and probably their physical and mental boosts.<br /> <br /> Dust sorcery which uses a combination of personal aura control and the external dust source to create various effects without the shaping effect of technology, generally not as efficient as a dust tech item but more versatile in a pinch. This would have several sub-disciplines such as external users vs. people who internalize dust before they use it. This would allow a person to gain a lot of effects but you'd need various units of dust of different varieties and mixes. This wouldn't be much like exalted sorcery, it'd be more like a Black Mage from Final Fantasy.<br /> <br /> Martial arts, several styles can probably be transported directly, especially the ones that don't involve physical transformations, although some would probably need to be modified slightly to be more weapon inclusive.<br /> <br /> Semblance, this is probably where the exigence stuff comes into play, because each aura user's semblance is likely to be a bit different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}